# Vercel and GitHub

When you complete a requested feature, bug fix, or refactor:

1. Verify the build. Run `npm run build`. It runs unit tests, then TypeScript, then the Vite bundle. Stop if any step fails.
2. Bump the release marker with `node scripts/bump-release.mjs` unless this change already updates `src/release.ts`. Include that file in the commit so one `git push` succeeds.
3. Commit the completed work on the current branch. Stage the files that belong to the change, including the release marker. Do not stage secrets (`.env`, credentials, keys).
4. Push to GitHub with `git push origin HEAD`. Do not force-push. Do not skip hooks.
5. Deploy with `npx vercel --prod --yes`.
6. Tell the user the production URL and that `origin` received the same commit.

```bash
npm run build
node scripts/bump-release.mjs
git add src/release.ts <changed files>
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Short why-focused message.

EOF
)"
git push origin HEAD
npx vercel --prod --yes
```
